        },
        {
          "step_number": 2,
          "title": "Step 2",
          "instruction": "Heat the oil in a pan and fry the onion for about 5 mins until softened. Add the garlic, chopped tomatoes, tomato pur\u00e9e, sweet paprika, chilli powder, sugar and a pinch of salt, then bring to the boil, stirring occasionally. Lower to a simmer and cook for 10 mins until pulpy. Can be kept chilled for up to 24 hrs."
        },
        {
          "step_number": 3,
          "title": "Step 3",
          "instruction": "step 2"
        },
        {
          "step_number": 4,
          "title": "Step 4",
          "instruction": "Heat oven to 200C/180C fan/gas 6. Pat the potatoes dry with kitchen paper, then tip into a roasting tin and toss in the olive oil and some seasoning. Roast for 40-50 mins until crisp and golden. Tip the potatoes into serving dishes and spoon over the tomato sauce. Sprinkle with some fresh parsley to serve."
        }
